/* ── Built-in tones ── */
"tone.warm" = "Warm";
"tone.warm.g" = "Genuinely receive what they said and move the relationship forward. Praise something specific, add a line of your own — but no flattery and no filler.";
"tone.thanks" = "Grateful";
"tone.thanks.g" = "Make the thanks concrete: what they did and what it meant to you. Don’t stop at “thanks”, and don’t overdo it until it becomes a burden.";
"tone.yes" = "Yes, on it";
"tone.yes.g" = "Agree cleanly and move things forward. Say exactly what you’ll do and by when — take it on gladly, but don’t vaguely promise the parts you can’t control.";
"tone.humor" = "Light";
"tone.humor.g" = "Defuse with lightness and a bit of self-deprecation. Jokes land on the situation, never the person — no sarcasm as a weapon. If it genuinely isn’t funny, don’t force it.";
"tone.comfort" = "Comforting";
"tone.comfort.g" = "For when they’re hurting. Receive the feeling first; don’t rush to advice or logic. Talk like a person — no slogans, no breezy “it’ll be fine”.";
"tone.decent" = "Gracious";
"tone.decent.g" = "Keep the relationship, leave room, easy for them to accept. Move things forward without litigating the past — but don’t silently agree to anything they left vague.";
"tone.ask" = "Clarify";
"tone.ask.g" = "Don’t commit while the information is thin. Ask the one or two things that decide it (what, by when, how much) and put the ball politely back in their court.";
"tone.needle" = "Pointed";
"tone.needle.g" = "Put the problem on the table, hold the line, neither fight nor fold. Speak in concrete facts, numbers and dates so they see the cost themselves. Stay polite throughout.";
"tone.table" = "Hard line";
"tone.table.g" = "State the rule, stop conceding, accept that this may end the relationship. Still only facts and consequences — no profanity, no personal attacks, no threats.";
"tone.cool" = "Hold off";
"tone.cool.g" = "Don’t commit, don’t take the bait, keep the decision yours. Short, calm, no explaining, no promises — buy yourself time.";

/* ── Built-in relationships ── */
"rel.none" = "Default";
"rel.family" = "Family";
"rel.family.g" = "You can’t opt out of family; anything said harshly you’ll live with for years. Be direct, set a boundary — but don’t drag up old grievances or pass judgment on who they are. Settle this one thing; keeping the relationship matters more than winning this round.";
"rel.friend" = "Friend";
"rel.friend.g" = "Equals, no hierarchy. You can be candid, jokes and self-deprecation are fine — but don’t use “we’re close” as licence to decide for them or to overstep.";
"rel.partner" = "Partner";
"rel.partner.g" = "Feelings weigh more than logic here. Receive how they feel before addressing the thing itself; no old grievances, no character verdicts, no silent treatment or ultimatums.";
"rel.client" = "Client";
"rel.client.g" = "There’s a commercial boundary. Hold scope, dates and price; polite but not free. Put in writing whatever needs to be, so a verbal aside doesn’t become an obligation.";
"rel.boss" = "Boss";
"rel.boss.g" = "There’s a power gap; pushing back head-on costs you. Don’t defy, but don’t silently accept a request they left vague either. Put cost, schedule and priority on the table and let them choose between options rather than you absorbing it alone.";

